__pycache__/
.dreamwork/status.json
# lint.py's append-only memo of the keys status.json has carried (#303) —
# gitignored because the file it describes is, and because it is a record of
# one target's history, not a schema anyone else should inherit.
.dreamwork/.status-keys
# derived at plugin resolution; which plugins resolve is a property
# of the machine, so a committed copy would be another target's truth
.dreamwork/plugin-commands.json
.dreamwork/watch-events.log
# every submission as it arrived, raw and unvalidated (#199). Ephemeral in the
# same sense as the events log — a recovery record for HIM, not project
# history — and it holds whatever he typed, so it is the last file that should
# ever be pushed anywhere.
.dreamwork/submissions.log
# Durable user-event journal (#263). Machine-local per target; holds exact
# payload bytes. WAL and SHM sidecars share the prefix.
.dreamwork/user-events.sqlite3
.dreamwork/user-events.sqlite3-wal
.dreamwork/user-events.sqlite3-shm
# #294: the ledger store is machine-local (C1 — the same trust boundary as
# the journal); cross-clone history is the committed text export (T3), a
# later deployment choice. The cutover's own backup dir is likewise local.
.dreamwork/ledger.sqlite3
.dreamwork/ledger.sqlite3-wal
.dreamwork/ledger.sqlite3-shm
.dreamwork/migration-backup/
# main-dreamer pace for this host (#290) — operational posture, not a
# portable project default (unlike watch-tint). Migration
# 2026-07-27-01-run-mode.md tells targets the same.
.dreamwork/run-mode
# #473: the dashboard's per-entry "when did this question last change" store.
# Machine-local by the same argument as run-mode above -- it records what THIS
# dashboard has seen, so committing it would assert another machine's history.
.dreamwork/question-sigs.json
# #387: the ledger-lint hook's last-seen mtime snapshot (Bash route). Same
# argument as question-sigs.json — it records what THIS machine's hook has
# seen, and a deleted copy costs one silent re-seed, never data.
.dreamwork/.ledger-lint-mtimes.json
# and the three-axis posture beside it (#445): same properties for the same
# reasons — machine-local, re-read every tick, and it describes THIS host's
# posture rather than the project's, so committing it would export one
# machine's settings to every checkout.
.dreamwork/posture
# The coordinator inbox: every line points at a report under /tmp, so the file
# is worthless the moment the session ends — all 8 of today's entries name
# paths that will not exist tomorrow. Same argument that ignores status.json
# and run-mode: it describes a running process, so committing it would be a lie
# as it landed. It was merely UNTRACKED until 2026-07-27, which is worse than
# either choice: it showed as `??` in every `git status`, and that is exactly
# the output used to decide whether a finished agent's worktree still holds
# unsaved work.
.dreamwork/inbox.md
# The same two files one directory down: a guard that drives the composer or
# answers a question for real makes the server write into the FROZEN fixture.
# The write is correct behaviour being exercised; the patterns above are
# anchored to the repo root and do not reach it, so they would sit untracked
# in every `git status` waiting for a careless `git add -A`.
dev/capture/fixture/.dreamwork/watch-events.log
dev/capture/fixture/.dreamwork/submissions.log
dev/capture/fixture/.dreamwork/run-mode
# lint.py's memo of which status.json keys this target has carried (#303).
# It describes a gitignored file and is per-target by construction, so
# committing it would import one machine's key set as another's baseline.
dev/capture/fixture/.dreamwork/.status-keys

# #526: the applied-ledger — consume writes one monotonic marker per drained
# receipt (the exactly-once proof). Machine-local by the same C1 argument as
# the ledger store; committing it would assert another machine's drain history.
# The .lock is the mutex the consume verb holds during a drain.
.dreamwork/applied.md
.dreamwork/applied.md.lock
# #504: the topic-chat transcript store — append-only turns per chat, keyed by
# the journal receipt id of the human's send. Machine-local conversational truth
# (the #229 ruling: chats gitignored by default; a cross-clone export is a later
# explicit act, never a `git add -f`). Same C1 boundary as submissions.log.
.dreamwork/chats-v1/

# worktrees for isolated dreamer spikes
.worktrees/

# harness-local runtime state — task backends and browser automation are
# session ephemera, not project content
.pi/
.playwright-mcp/
*.tmp.*

# #653 — the pinned dev-time bundler for `just build-client`. Gitignored like
# every other node dependency here (the browser guards resolve Playwright the
# same way): what is COMMITTED is the build's OUTPUT, client/dist/, because
# `just deploy` ships committed state and the dashboard must come up with no
# node at all. `npm ci` in dev/build restores this from package-lock.json.
dev/build/node_modules/
